    <ferc:StatementAboutImportantChangesDuringTheQuarterYearTextBlock id="f-290" contextRef="c-20">&lt;p&gt;1. Not Applicable&lt;br /&gt;2. Not Applicable&lt;br /&gt;3. Not Applicable&lt;br /&gt;4. Not Applicable&lt;br /&gt;5. Not Applicable&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</ferc:StatementAboutImportantChangesDuringTheQuarterYearTextBlock>
    <ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="f-292" contextRef="c-20">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); font-size: small; text-align: justify"&gt;&lt;b style="font-weight: bolder; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-size: small"&gt;NOTE A - ORGANIZATION, OPERATIONS AND BASIS OF PRESENTATION:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 1rem; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); font-size: small"&gt;&lt;br style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); font-size: small"&gt;&lt;b style="font-weight: bolder; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;Organization.&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;Ba&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;you Bridge Pipeline, LLC (&amp;quot;Bayou Bridge&amp;quot;) is jointly owned by subsidiaries of Phillips 66 Partners LP (&amp;quot;Phillips 66&amp;quot;) and Energy Transfer LP (&amp;quot;Energy Transfer&amp;quot;). Phillips 66 holds a 40% interest in the joint venture and Energy Transfer holds a 60% interest.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 1rem; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); font-size: small"&gt;&lt;b style="font-weight: bolder; background-color: initial; text-align: inherit"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 1rem; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); font-size: small"&gt;&lt;b style="font-weight: bolder; background-color: initial; text-align: inherit"&gt;Operations&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style="background-color: initial; text-align: inherit"&gt;. B&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="background-color: initial; text-align: inherit"&gt;ayou Bridge is a Delaware company engaged in the transportation of crude oil. The Bayou Bridge Pipeline consists of 49 miles of 30-inch pipeline from Nederland, Texas to Lake Charles, Louisiana, and 163 miles of 24-inch pipeline from Lake Charles, Louisiana to St. James, Louisiana. Bayou Bridge Pipeline has a capacity of approximately 480 MBbls/d of light and heavy crude oil from different sources to the St. James crude oil hub, which is home to important refineries located in the Gulf Coast region.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 1rem; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); font-size: small"&gt;&lt;b style="font-weight: bolder; background-color: initial; text-align: inherit"&gt;Regulation.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style="background-color: initial; text-align: inherit"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;Bayou Bridge crude oil transportation activities are subject to regulation by the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission (&amp;quot;FERC&amp;quot;) and various state authorities. Regulatory bodies exercise statutory authority over matters such as rates and underlying accounting practices, as well as rate making agreements with customers.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 1rem; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); font-size: small"&gt;&lt;span lang="en-US" style="color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-style: normal; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; text-decoration: none; font-weight: bold"&gt;Basis of Presentation.&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); display: inline !important; float: none"&gt;B&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span lang="en-US" style="color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small; font-style: normal; font-weight: normal; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; text-decoration: none"&gt;ayou Bridge's financial statements have been prepared in accordance with accounting requirements of the FERC, as set forth in the applicable Uniform System of Accounts and published accounting releases, which is a comprehensive basis of accounting other than accounting principles generally accepted in the United States of America (&amp;quot;GAAP&amp;quot;). The most significant differences between GAAP and the financial statement presented herein are: (1) classification of certain accounts on the balance sheet, statement of income and the statement of cash flows and (2) use of the FERC approved depreciation rates.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 13.2pt; margin-bottom: 1rem; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); font-size: small; text-align: justify"&gt;&lt;b style="font-weight: bolder; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-size: small"&gt;NOTE B - SUMMARY OF SIGNIFICANT ACCOUNTING POLICIES AND OTHER MATTERS:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 1rem; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); font-size: small"&gt;&lt;b style="font-weight: bolder; background-color: initial; text-align: inherit"&gt;&lt;span&gt;Use of Estimates&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 1rem; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: inherit; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); font-size: small"&gt;&lt;span style="background-color: initial; text-align: inherit"&gt;The preparation of financial statements requires management to make estimates and assumptions that affect the reported amounts of assets and liabilities and disclosure of contingent assets and liabilities at the date of the financial statements and the reported amounts of revenues and expenses during the reporting period. A&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="background-color: initial; text-align: inherit"&gt;ctual results could differ from those estimates.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 1rem; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); font-size: small"&gt;&lt;b style="font-weight: bolder; background-color: initial; text-align: inherit"&gt;&lt;span&gt;Cash and Cash Equivalents&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 1rem; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: inherit; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); font-size: small"&gt;&lt;span style="background-color: initial; text-align: inherit"&gt;Cash equivalents consist of highly liquid investments, which are readily convertible into cash and have original maturities of three months or less. The cash deposits and temporary cash investments are placed with high credit quality financial institutions. A&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="background-color: initial; text-align: inherit"&gt;t times, Bayou Bridge's cash and cash equivalents may be uninsured or in deposit accounts that exceed the Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation insurance limit.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 1rem; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); font-size: small"&gt;&lt;b style="font-weight: bolder; background-color: initial; text-align: inherit"&gt;&lt;span&gt;Property, Plant and Equipment&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 1rem; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: inherit; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); font-size: small"&gt;&lt;span style="background-color: initial; text-align: inherit"&gt;Bayou Bridge capitalizes expenditures related to property, plant and equipment that have a useful life greater than one year for (1) assets purchased or constructed; (2) existing assets that are replaced or improved; or (3) land regardless of cost. D&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="background-color: initial; text-align: inherit"&gt;uring construction, Bayou Bridge capitalizes direct costs, such as labor, materials and overhead. B&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="background-color: initial; text-align: inherit"&gt;ayou Bridge records property, plant and equipment at its original cost. Depreciation is computed on a composite straight line method at the FERC authorized rates based on the expected economic lives of the various classes of assets.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 1rem; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); font-size: small"&gt;&lt;b style="font-weight: bolder; background-color: initial; text-align: inherit"&gt;&lt;span&gt;Accounts Receivable and Allowance for Credit Losses&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 1rem; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: inherit; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); font-size: small"&gt;&lt;span style="background-color: initial; text-align: inherit"&gt;Accounts receivable are carried at the amount owed by customers less an allowance for credit losses, if deemed necessary. B&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="background-color: initial; text-align: inherit"&gt;ayou Bridge evaluates the collectability of accounts receivable based on review of a specific customer's ability to meet its financial obligation or as a result of changes in the overall aging of accounts receivable.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 1rem; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: inherit; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); font-size: small"&gt;&lt;span style="background-color: initial; text-align: inherit"&gt;Bayou Bridge's allowance for credit losses was not material as of December 31, 2025 and 2024.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 1rem; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); font-size: small"&gt;&lt;b style="font-weight: bolder; background-color: initial; text-align: inherit"&gt;&lt;span&gt;Revenue Recognition&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 1rem; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); font-size: small"&gt;&lt;b style="font-weight: bolder; background-color: initial; text-align: inherit"&gt;Contract Balances with Customers&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); font-size: small"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Bayou Bridge satisfies its obligations by transferring goods or services in exchange for consideration from customers. The timing of performance may differ from the timing that the associated consideration is received from the customer, thus resulting in the recognition of a contract liability.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 1rem; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: inherit; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); font-size: small"&gt;&lt;span style="background-color: initial; text-align: inherit"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 1rem; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: inherit; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); font-size: small"&gt;&lt;span style="background-color: initial; text-align: inherit"&gt;Bayou Bridge recognizes a contract liability if the customer's payment of consideration precedes Bayou Bridge's fulfillment of the performance obligations. C&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="background-color: initial; text-align: inherit"&gt;ertain contracts contain provisions requiring customers to pay a fixed fee for a right to use Bayou Bridge's assets, but allow customers to apply such fees against services to be provided at a future point in time. T&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="background-color: initial; text-align: inherit"&gt;hese amounts are reflected as deferred revenue until the customer applies the deficiency fees to services provided or becomes unable to use the fees as payment for future services due to expiration of the contractual period the fees can be applied or physical inability of the customer to utilize the fees due to capacity constraints.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 1rem; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); font-size: small"&gt;&lt;b style="font-weight: bolder; background-color: initial; text-align: inherit"&gt;Performance Obligations&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); font-size: small"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;At contract inception, Bayou Bridge assesses the goods and services promised in its contracts with customers and identifies a performance obligation for each promise to transfer a good or service that is distinct. Revenue is recognized when (or as) the performance obligations are satisfied, that is, when the customer obtains control of the good or service.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 1rem; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: inherit; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); font-size: small"&gt;&lt;span style="background-color: initial; text-align: inherit"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 1rem; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: inherit; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); font-size: small"&gt;&lt;span style="background-color: initial; text-align: inherit"&gt;Bayou Bridge generally does not own the crude oil that it transports or stores.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 1rem; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); font-size: small"&gt;&lt;b style="font-weight: bolder; background-color: initial; text-align: inherit"&gt;&lt;span&gt;Income Taxes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 1rem; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: inherit; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); font-size: small"&gt;&lt;span style="background-color: initial; text-align: inherit"&gt;Bayou Bridge is a limited liability company that has elected to be treated as a partnership for income tax purposes. A&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="background-color: initial; text-align: inherit"&gt;ccordingly, the tax effects of Bayou Bridge's activities generally accrue to its members.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 1rem; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); font-size: small"&gt;&lt;b style="font-weight: bolder; background-color: initial; text-align: inherit"&gt;&lt;span&gt;Environmental Remediation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 1rem; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: inherit; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); font-size: small"&gt;&lt;span style="background-color: initial; text-align: inherit"&gt;Bayou Bridge accrues environmental remediation costs for work at identified sites where an assessment has indicated that cleanup costs are probable and reasonably estimable. Such accruals are undiscounted and are based on currently available information, estimated timing of remedial actions and related inflation assumptions, existing technology and presently enacted laws and regulations. If a range of probable environmental cleanup costs exists for an identified site, the minimum of the range is accrued unless some other point or points in the range are more likely, in which case the most likely amount in this range is accrued.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); text-align: justify; font-size: 10pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;b style="font-weight: bolder"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;NOTE C - COMMITMENT AND CONTINGENCIES:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); text-align: justify; font-size: 10pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;b style="font-weight: bolder"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 1rem; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: inherit; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1)"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; background-color: initial; text-align: inherit"&gt;Bayou Bridge may be subject to various legal proceedings and claims that arise in the ordinary course of business. In the opinion of management, the amount of any ultimate liability with respect to any such actions will not materially affect the company's financial position or results of operations.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 13.2pt; margin-bottom: 1rem; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); font-size: small; text-align: justify"&gt;&lt;b style="font-weight: bolder; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-size: small"&gt;NOTE D - RELATED PARTY TRANSACTIONS:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class="_Normal_" style="margin: 0 0 1rem; font-size: 14px; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; color: rgba(51, 51, 51, 1); font-family: Roboto, &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, GeezaPro, &amp;quot;DejaVu Serif&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;sans-serif&amp;quot;, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); line-height: 18.4px"&gt;&lt;span lang="en-US" style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; text-decoration: none; line-height: 15.3333px"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(51, 51, 51, 1); font-family: Arial; font-size: 13.3333px; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); float: none; display: inline !important"&gt;Bayou Bridge p&lt;/span&gt;ays Energy Transfer an annual fixed operating fee as reimbursement for providing certain services including business development, legal services, accounting and financial reporting, human resource services, and other as defined in the o&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span lang="en-US" style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial; font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; text-decoration: none; line-height: 15.3333px"&gt;perating agreement. The fixed operating fee is escalated annually and is Energy Transfer's sole reimbursement and compensation for any allocation of Energy Transfer's or its affiliates' overhead related to the services.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class="_Normal_" style="margin: 0 0 1rem; font-size: 14px; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: inherit; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; color: rgba(51, 51, 51, 1); font-family: Roboto, &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, GeezaPro, &amp;quot;DejaVu Serif&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;sans-serif&amp;quot;, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); line-height: 18.4px"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt; background-color: initial; text-align: inherit"&gt;The fixed operating fee was $1.4 million for each of the years ended December 31, 2025 and 2024.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 13.2pt; margin-bottom: 1rem; color: rgba(73, 80, 87, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); font-size: small; text-align: justify"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock>
    <ferc:DescriptionOfAssetsOrOfTransaction id="f-294" contextRef="c-67">Affiliate receivables for services</ferc:DescriptionOfAssetsOrOfTransaction>
    <ferc:DescriptionOfAssetsOrOfTransaction id="f-295" contextRef="c-68">Affiliate receivables for services and materials</ferc:DescriptionOfAssetsOrOfTransaction>
    <ferc:DescriptionOfAssetsOrOfTransaction id="f-296" contextRef="c-69">Minor accounts, less than $500,000</ferc:DescriptionOfAssetsOrOfTransaction>
    <ferc:NameOrClassOfDebtors id="f-297" contextRef="c-67">Energy Transfer Crude Marketing</ferc:NameOrClassOfDebtors>
